 "findings": {
  "resp_cmd": "astk response_data (owner_7 -> 512 pv slices + 64 joins, 95 b each in the census) and pvw ctl cmd are ALREADY one registered 289-b column trunk in RTL (qkd_pvw_die_t / pv_trunk_gen.py: CL -> per block row X station + 2 pass-through M stations -> CP -> K per column group -> S/R -> 8 bank slices). The census treats relays as transparent and flattens it into 4,800 independent 0.4-13-mm lanes (1.08M bit-mm, 20% of the die); it also attributes the same K bits to every upstream source (EN, WN and ctl each 95 b a slice; the real K->slice wires are 56-58 b). Rewrite: trie of the census relay paths, wire widths from the dump bundles, pass-through stations collapsed (1,042 dropped, 168 kept: 4 entry lands, CL, one X a block row, K taps): 752 lanes, 69,760 b, 36.7k bit-mm. No RTL change needed beyond dropping the M / CP / S pass-through stations (pv_trunk_gen at 1.2-mm hops); static, fixed path a sink.",
  "head": "head dr_o / f_t0-3 / kp / kp_o / cr_o: one-hop leaf-to-leaf wires inside each 1,030 x 540-um head (front 4 -> stin 16 -> lane8 16 -> stk 16 -> ktree), 150-400 um straight, sinks 135 um apart taking disjoint slices (except q). Not a broadcast over distance: a registered chain T2 -> front3..0 carries 1559/1303/1047/791 = 4,700 b-hops vs the star 4 x 809 = 3,236, so chaining adds wire. Per head the straight local demand is 3.73M track-um on M8 (54% of the footprint) / 1.87M on M9 (27%); the plan routes them at 6x that (22M / 23M) because the 250-um span bins and +-1.5-mm band shifts inflate 150-um lanes. Sensitivity (plan.py Tracks span 50 um, nothing else changed): head ovf lanes 10,433 -> 2,735 (basis) / 10,009 -> 1,457 (after). Fix belongs in the planner (span resolution / local-layer M6-M7 assignment for intra-cluster wires), not RTL.",
  "hst_t2_ti_b": "hst t2 ti_b -> 4 fronts = the head input fan-out (T2 sits 150-180 um above the 4 fronts): same as head. hst g -> t1 -> t2 / ftg is already a registered chain (0 overflow). One structural lever: --head-qslice.",
  "head_qslice": "RTL what-if: front g serves the 4 lanes whose BF16 Q fragment comes from q_data half (fragment j = t%4: j 0/2 <- q[255:0], j 1/3 <- q[511:256]), so T2 -> front q_data 512 -> 256 b (512 lanes, -131k b). Needs ot_qkh_head_frontq_native (q_data_in 256, f_t lane mapping) + head lane permutation (head_lane_perm / head plan) changes; rounding / pairing per element unchanged (bit-exact by construction, gate by the head bench)."
 },
